    "result_text": "The full test suite passes. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What the change does\n\nOn owner creation (`POST /api/owners`), the response now carries a `bulkSignupWarning` boolean: **true** when more than 80 owners had already been created for that owner's (business-day) registration date at the time of creation, **false** otherwise. The value is captured at create time and persisted, so it reads back consistently via `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n## Files changed\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema (regenerates `OwnerDto` with getter/setter).\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 new persisted `Boolean bulkSignupWarning` field (`bulk_signup_warning` column) with getter/setter, following the `namesakeCount` pattern.\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 ignore `bulkSignupWarning` on the `OwnerFieldsDto \u2192 Owner` mapping (it's derived server-side, like `namesakeCount`); the `Owner \u2192 OwnerDto` direction maps it automatically.\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 80` and a `bulkSignupWarning(registrationDate)` helper that counts existing owners on that effective business day and returns `count > 80`; `addOwner` sets it before persisting. The count reflects state *before* the new owner is saved, matching the existing daily-limit rule's accumulation path.\n5. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `bulk_signup_warning` column (tests use hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the DDL is required).\n\nVerification: `AcceptanceTest.coreNoBulkWarningUnderThreshold` (the false branch) passes, and the full `mvn test` run is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
